            },
            "body": "**Light review — LGTM**\n\nThe fix correctly closes a misrouting bug: a `*ForTokenClassification` model whose `auto_map` also exports `AutoModelForCausalLM` (a common multitask config) previously matched the causal-LM entry and was routed down the causal-LM bridge path. The new `_get_architecture_class_name_via_auto_map` guard returns `None` for token-classification architectures so resolution falls through to the correct token-classification bridge. Both call sites (`_causal_lm_architecture` and `_validate_config`) are updated consistently, and the added test exercises the exact scenario (bridge selects `PreTrainedTokenClassification`, `score.weight`/`score.bias` mappings present).\n\nMinor observation (non-blocking): the helper name is generic but only special-cases `ForTokenClassification`. A `*ForMaskedLM` architecture whose `auto_map` also contains `AutoModelForCausalLM` would still be misrouted the same way. If that combination is possible for supported masked-LM models, consider generalizing the guard or documenting why it is token-classification-only.\n\n**Suggested test cases:**\n- test_token_classification_config_with_multitask_auto_map_uses_task_bridge (added — covers the fix)\n- A negative/regression case asserting a pure causal-LM `auto_map` (no `ForTokenClassification` architecture) still resolves to the causal-LM class name via `auto_map`, guarding against over-broad `None` returns.\n\nNo perf tests impacted.",
